+  pages, onboarding logo text, scale and topology panels, data-transfer, GitHub connect
+  errors, issue fixtures). Keys, comments and identifiers were not touched.
+- Dashboard tests re-pointed at the new strings (nine files); i18n-parity MISSING_BASELINE
+  for `brand` is 45 because a one-string namespace is counted per character.
+- CLI: apps/cli program description, help text, prompts, spinner and doctor/uninstall
+  output, and the package.json description now say FreeBuild. Binary name `openship`
+  and the package name are unchanged.
+- Compose: header comments of docker-compose.yml and docker/docker-compose.yml. Service
+  names, container names (`openship-edge`), the compose project name and volumes are
+  unchanged because the CLI, the API and edge detection look them up by name.
+- Default names: the mail test mailbox display name (apps/api test-mailbox.service.ts)
+  is "FreeBuild Test".
+- Deploy status goes through claim_deploy. `packages/platform/src/engine/modules/
+  deployments/netie-claim.ts` mirrors Netie `scripts/freebuild_honesty.py`
+  report_deploy: a simulated deploy, a constructed URL or a missing observed URL is
+  UNCLAIMED; with NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL set the claim also needs parent and child run
+  ids and an allowed=true answer from `${NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL}/api/crew/gate` (kind
+  service, id freebuild, intent leave), failing closed on any error. The verdict is
+  written with the "ready" outcome as `meta.netieClaim`; `GET /api/deployments/:id`
+  and the list return `live` and `netieClaim`; the project payload carries
+  `activeDeploymentLive`; the dashboard pill reads "Deployed, unclaimed" (new
+  ProjectStatus `unclaimed`) until a LIVE claim exists. No upstream path observes
+  the URL today (docker and bare return none, cloud and compose compose one from a
+  hostname), so every deploy is UNCLAIMED until an observation step exists.
+  Tests: netie-claim.test.ts (9), apps/api netie-claim-lifecycle and
+  netie-claim-api.contract (9), dashboard project-status-claim.test.ts (3).
+- Vendor assets: every cdn.oblien.com reference and the Gellix and SF Arabic fonts
+  removed from the dashboard, the web site, the email app, the desktop loading
+  screen, the screenshot script and the docs; the two vendored Gellix woff2 files
